HOW TO USE
1. Copy this file and rename it to the meeting date, e.g. 2026-10-02-meeting.md
   (it must end in .md, not .md.example — the filename becomes the page URL).
2. Fill in the fields between the --- lines. Dates are YYYY-MM-DD.
   location, duration, attendees, summary and nextMeeting are optional: delete a line to hide it.
3. Write the minutes below in Markdown: "## " makes a section heading, "- " a bullet,
   and the | table | format above makes a table.
4. Save — with `npm run dev` running the page updates on its own.
